@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Connect your organisation";
}

<h1>Connect your organisation</h1>

<p class="lead"><strong>Who can do this:</strong> a Global Administrator or Privileged Role
Administrator in your Microsoft Entra tenant.</p>

<h2 class="h5">What we ask for and why</h2>

<table class="table align-middle">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th scope="col">Permission</th>
            <th scope="col">What it lets us read</th>
            <th scope="col">What it does not do</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td>Read organisation information</td>
            <td>Your purchased licences and subscription renewal dates</td>
            <td>Nothing about individual users</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>Read all users' basic profiles</td>
            <td>Which licences are assigned to which people, and whether accounts are active</td>
            <td>Cannot read email, files, messages or passwords; cannot change anything</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<p>
    We never buy, assign or remove licences with these permissions. You can revoke access at any
    time from <strong>Entra admin centre &rarr; Enterprise applications &rarr; MLCP &rarr;
    Permissions</strong>.
</p>

<h2 class="h5">Steps</h2>
<ol>
    <li>Click <strong>Connect as administrator</strong>.</li>
    <li>Sign in with your admin account. Multi-factor authentication may be required.</li>
    <li>Review the permissions and click <strong>Accept</strong>.</li>
    <li>You will return here. Discovery takes one to two minutes.</li>
</ol>

<p class="text-muted">
    <strong>If you are not an administrator:</strong> use <em>Send request to my admin</em> and we
    will email them this page with a one-click link.
</p>

<a class="btn btn-primary" asp-controller="Onboarding" asp-action="Index">Back to connection status</a>
